cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AROC: a parallel domain-modeling effort on an event-sourced chassis"
message: "If you use AROC in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gursoy
    given-names: Doga
    affiliation: Argonne National Laboratory
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0080-8101"
repository-code: "https://github.com/xmap/aroc"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-15"
keywords:
  - event-sourcing
  - domain-driven-design
  - bounded-contexts
  - hexagonal-architecture
  - model-context-protocol
abstract: >-
  AROC is a parallel modeling effort sharing the architecture of its sibling
  project CORA: event-sourced bounded contexts over Postgres, hexagonal ports
  and adapters, and equivalent REST and agent-protocol (MCP) API surfaces
  backed by a single handler per command. The chassis is inherited; the
  subject of the work is the set of domains modeled on top of it. The name
  mirrors CORA, as does the reading: CORA is Continuously Overpromised,
  Rarely Automated, and AROC is Automated Rarely, Overpromised Continuously.
